cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PyTES, please cite it as below."
title: "PyTES: Python Thermal Energy Storage"
abstract: >-
  PyTES is a library of models and tools for thermal energy storage (heat batteries),
  built on PyBaMM. It covers storage in which a heat transfer fluid flows through or
  around a separate storage medium, such as finned-tube phase-change material units and
  packed beds of encapsulated phase-change material, with models that share one
  interface, conserve energy exactly and are validated against analytical solutions and
  measurements.
type: software
authors:
